From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: a733: set clock-latency-ns on the CPU OPPs from the measured park

What. clock-latency-ns on every operating point of both CPU OPP tables:
45000 ns on cluster0 (A55, cpu0-5), 38000 ns on cluster1 (A76, cpu6-7).

Why. `arm64-dts-a733-cpu-opp-tables-and-supply` left the property out on purpose: the vendor's 244144 ns is
1/4096 s, a constant found in unrelated DTs, and the UM gives only a 1.5 ms
lock bound (Table 4-2), so the only honest value was a measurement nobody
had. It was measured: `clk-sunxi-ng-a733-cpu-pll-park-timing`'s notifier times one CPU PLL change from
PRE_RATE_CHANGE to POST_RATE_CHANGE -- the whole time the cluster is off its
PLL, the clk framework included. On the 6 GiB board, 6.18.36-t0036 with the clusters
parked on CPU_BACK_PLL (`clk-sunxi-ng-a733-park-core-clusters-on-cpu-back-pll` + the TF-A patch
`allwinner-a733-enable-cpu-back-pll`), 2026-09-23, tracer-free,
under a bursty load: A55 median 39.2 us, p99 44.9 us; A76 median 33.5 us,
p99 37.2 us. The
values are those p99s rounded up to the microsecond.

Who reads it: of.c:896 per OPP, the table maximum returned by
dev_pm_opp_get_max_transition_latency() (core.c:318), added to the volt
latency (196 us, `arm64-dts-a733-cpu-opp-tables-and-supply`'s ramp delay) and used by cpufreq-dt as
cpuinfo.transition_latency (cpufreq-dt.c:105-114). schedutil's rate limit
follows as 1.5 x latency (cpufreq.c:552-555): 294 us before, 361 us with
this patch. schedutil's tunables are global here, so the A55 policy's value
serves both clusters.

What it does not cover: a boot chain without the TF-A patch
`allwinner-a733-enable-cpu-back-pll` leaves
CPU_BACK_PLL off, `clk-sunxi-ng-a733-park-core-clusters-on-cpu-back-pll` then parks on the 26 MHz DCXO and a change takes
~322/153 us (A55/A76 median). The kernel says so at probe (`clk-sunxi-ng-a733-park-core-clusters-on-cpu-back-pll`'s warning);
this value is for the boot chain this recipe builds.

On the board (the 6 GiB board, 6.18.36-t0999, boot chain with the TF-A patch `allwinner-a733-enable-cpu-back-pll`,
2026-09-23): cpuinfo_transition_latency 241000 ns (policy0) and 234000 ns
(policy6) = 196 us + 45 / 38 us; schedutil rate_limit_us 361. Whether the rate limit needs more than this is still open; a pending test
on the 8 GiB board decides it.

For a comparison run without it: A7S_SKIP_PATCHES=arm64-dts-a733-cpu-opp-clock-latency-measured.

Assisted-by: Claude
